00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.670 align:start position:0%
 
it's been about six months since apple  released their new macbook pros and i've  not only been putting them through a lot  of testing here in the office but also  at home because i finally upgraded from  my old 2018 intel 15 inch model to the  new 16 inch m1 max macbook pro and i  definitely have some thoughts after six  months to say the least and now that we  finally released our one month review of  apple's new mac studio i can now give  you guys my thoughts on which machine is  the better buy the macbook or the studio  but first i wanted to share my at-home  experience with my new 16-inch macbook  pro so let's jump right into that first  of all one of the biggest advantages i  noticed going from my old 15-inch intel  model was the increase in battery life  since i'm now finally able to use it for  multiple sessions without having to plug  it in and my absolute favorite new  feature is the new display because it  has multiple advantages over previous  macbook displays like the fact that it  comes with the super slim bezels because  that's something i notice every time i  use it and after six months the notch  has literally had zero negative impact  on my experience i barely even notice it  anymore but the main game changer for  everyday use has been the 120 hertz pro  motion display because now that it's  been six months chrome and safari now  properly support 120hz browsing and  everything just feels so smooth and  responsive because of it perfectly  matching my 120hz experience on my  iphone and not even looking at promotion  the web browsing itself is super snappy  compared to old intel max because of the  m1 max chip having really high single  core performance so there are no  stutters or issues whatsoever especially  thanks to the super fast 32 gigs of  unified memory and the equally fast  built-in ssds i also basically never  hear the fans on this new macbook pro  which is an awesome change compared to  my old intel macbook pro which would  sometimes spin up the fans while even  just browsing the web now another one of  my favorite features on the new macbook  pro is the absolutely incredible speaker  system that has graduated from laptop's  speaker level to sound like an actual  set of dedicated desktop speakers now in  terms of performance i honestly think i  went a bit overkill by going with the 32  core m1 max chip because i don't think  i've gotten even close to maxing it out  in my workloads for example i often use  my macbook to create thumbnails at home  when we're falling a bit behind at the  office and it has absolutely zero issues  in photoshop and i also did a bit of  video editing and i haven't ever felt  like my mind is working faster than this  macbook pro so the performance is great  now the reason i got the 32 core m1 max  model was first of all for future  proofing and second of all because i  wanted to make sure i had the absolute  most graphics performance for gaming to  try and take advantage of the 120 hertz  display but now that i'm a father of two  i don't really play that often anymore  so i honestly think i would have been  completely fine with the base m1 pro  chip because it's enough to handle  everything i'm currently doing on it so  my experience after six months has been  absolutely amazing and it's the happiest  i've ever been with a single mac product  except for one issue  the mini led display  yes the new display can reach up to 1600  nits of brightness while viewing or  editing hdr content which is awesome but  when you're using it normally like when  you're browsing the web is limited to  just the standard 500 nits but with the  new vivid app for mac you can get the  brightness up to 1 000 nits all the time  which is super useful for outdoor use or  any bright environment and know they're  not sponsoring this video now my main  issue with the mini led display is  blooming where you can see a glow behind  bright objects on the display especially  in the dark now while you're looking  directly at the display you can't really  notice it but the blooming problem  became annoying to me when i watched the  movie dune with my wife while on the  couch and i was looking at the display  from the side and that's where blooming  problems became really apparent but  other than that the mini led display has  been great so overall my six month  experience with my new 16-inch macbook  pro has been awesome but now let's  switch over to a more high performance  oriented outlook and compare it to the  new max studio which can now be packed  with the m1 ultra chip being the main  advantage over the macbook pro first of  all the base price of the mac studio for  only 2 000 is very impressive because it  comes with the m1 max chip built in  which is exactly how much it costs for  the cheapest m1 pro chip in the 14 inch  macbook pro but to make the comparison  as fair as possible between the mac  studio and the more expensive 16 inch  macbook pro we configured both of them  with exactly the same specs and the  macbook pro ends up being eleven hundred  dollars more expensive than the mac  studio however you also have to factor  in the fact that you'll still need to  buy a mouse a keyboard and a display for  the mac studio which could get expensive  very quickly if you decide to go for  apple's own magic accessories and new  studio display which together come out  to around nineteen hundred dollars but  just to give the max studio the benefit  of the doubt let's give it a much less  expensive display like the 27 inch asus  pro art 4k display that of course  doesn't match up in terms of the refresh  rate but it's still a good option and  then we'll add in another 100  for a basic mouse and keyboard and now  with those changes the macbook pro is  only 500 more expensive than this mac  studio setup 3100 instead of 2600 so  let's get into the performance  comparison we tested various workflows  and apps from all kinds of benchmarks  like cinebench r23 graphics tests like  gfx bench and a lot of real world tests  like xcode photo editing in adobe  lightroom classic and various video  editing tests and to our surprise the  macbook pro actually beat out the mac  studio in a bunch of different tests  which didn't make any sense at all so  it's pretty clear that apple is not  allowing the m1 max max studio to  perform even an ounce better than the m1  max macbook pro even though it's a  desktop which is extremely disappointing  so with that said paying 500 more for  the macbook pro setup actually seems  like a much better value because you can  actually take it on the go wherever you  want which is a massive value add  compared to the mac studio which  absolutely must be connected to the wall  now of course the biggest downside of  the macbook pro is that you can't get  the m1 ultra chip which is currently  only available in the mac studio and  it's now the main reason so many people  are thinking about buying the mac studio  so here are the specs of the machines  we're comparing with the 4 000 max  studio with a binned 48 core gpu and 64  gigs of ram and by adding in the 600  accessories it is now 1100  more expensive than the higher end 32  core gpu m1 max macbook pro with 32 gigs  of ram now the first point i want to  make is that everyday performance for  common things like web browsing barely  improves by two percent because basic  tasks are based on single core  performance which doesn't really change  much between the m1 max and the ultra  now multi-core performance is where the  ultra shines because you're getting 91  more power for 31 more cash which is a  great investment but translating that to  real world performance the xcode  programming benchmark was only 22 faster  because the m1 max was already  incredibly fast due to the unified  memory architecture so it's not really  worth it for programmers but the real  winner in terms of performance was  exporting photos in lightroom classic  where the ultra was almost twice as fast  making the extra 1100 very worth it but  in terms of actual editing smoothness  the m1 max was already perfect for us  now we ended up creating a panorama  using lightroom and here the ultra was  only 23 faster so it wasn't really worth  it now moving over to the graphics side  in terms of raw gpu power and 3d mark  wildlife extreme the ultra got around 45  more fps which honestly isn't too bad  for spending 1100 more but going into  some real world stuff like the blender  bmw cycles render it was only 20 faster  which i honestly don't think is worth  the extra 31 cash because you're also  sacrificing portability with the mac  studio but the absolute worst results  that we found were in terms of video  editing where exporting common h.264 and  h.265 videos led to basically no gains  at all because apparently the extra set  of media engines in the ultra cannot be  utilized at all right now and in terms  of playback smoothness the 24 core m1  max yeah not the 32 core already can run  15 streams of 4k hevc footage with extra  effects without dropping frames and we  even stacked a huge amount of effects  color corrections luts masks and  animated titles on a single stream of  heavier canon r5 footage and it didn't  drop any frames showing that almost  nobody will be able to get extra  playback smoothness from the m1 ultra so  because of that we decided to export 8k  red raw which doesn't support encoders  and decoders and the m1 ultramax studio  was only 14  faster definitely not worth the extra  1100  it was only when we exported a five  minute 4k pro res raw video to prores  that we finally started seeing the  encoders and decoders being used  properly giving us a 33  improvement and then in our final 8k  canon raw to 4k hvc torture test the m1  ultra was only 22 faster than the  macbook pro which is just so  disappointing compared to our initial  expectations now if you're wondering why  the ultra isn't performing that well  it's because the gpu has a major  hardware bottleneck that limits the top  end performance of the gpu and slows  everything down and unfortunately this  isn't going to change until apps get  optimized or until apple releases the m2  ultra with a fix for the hardware issue  so with all that said i would honestly  say that the m1 ultra isn't worth it for  the majority of people out there and  because of that the m1 max macbook pro  just leveled up in terms of how much  value i think it has and i'm so happy i  made this purchase around six months ago  especially since i've been enjoying so  many of its other features so hopefully  you guys enjoyed my six month review of  the 16 inch macbook pro and if you did  go ahead and click the circle about to  subscribe for more videos like this one  and definitely check out one of those  two right over there including our other  comparisons thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video  [Music]

